This PR adds a behavior to proxy the (un)registering of Hotkeys to the hotkeys-js library, which has been added as a peer dependency.

Tests and documentation have been updated accordingly.

Example of a config, taken from the tests:

```js
connect() {
    useHotkeys(this, {
      hotkeys: {
        '/': {
          handler: 'singleKeyHandler'
        },
        'cmd+a': {
          handler: 'metaKeyHandler'
        },
        f: {
          handler: 'scopeHandler',
          options: {
            scope: 'files'
          }
        },
        b: {
          handler: 'inputHandler'
        },
        c: {
          handler: 'keyUpHandler',
          options: {
            keydown: false,
            keyup: true
          }
        },
        'ctrl-d': {
          handler: 'splitKeyHandler',
          options: {
            splitKey: '-'
          }
        }
      },
      filter: this.filter
    })
}
```

The MeasFrame class owns a MCFrame object which itself owns a copy of its parent MeasFrame. This causes problems with memory leaks and potential table being left open. This PR simply stores a pointer to the parent MeasFrame in the MCFrame.

This should solve #1111. After this change there are no more tables open and valgrind doesn't report more significant problems (there are still leaks related to LogIO, but those are not relevant here).

@aroffringa: of you can review this it would be great. Or maybe you can find a better solution based on the idea of this commit. Thanks!

